dzn: Share pipeline state objects between devices on one ID3D12Device

Creating a PSO runs the GPU driver's shader compiler, and a VkPipelineCache
hit only skips the NIR and DXIL steps before it. A Vulkan device is
created per instance, and when D3D12 returns an existing ID3D12Device
(D3D12_DEVICE_FACTORY_FLAG_ALLOW_RETURNING_EXISTING_DEVICE) several
instances end up on the same one: gfxstream, for example, creates an
instance for each Android process that draws, and those processes use
the same shaders for their UI.

Keep the PSOs created on an ID3D12Device in a table keyed by the contents
of the pipeline state stream, with the shader bytecode, input layout and
view instancing locations in place of their pointers and the root
signature as the object, which each entry holds a reference to. A
pipeline with the same stream then gets the existing PSO. The table is
released with the last device on that ID3D12Device and holds at most 4096
PSOs.

On an Intel Iris Plus 650 under WSL2, the third cold start of an Android
app found 7 of its 8 PSOs in the table, each one a 13-30 ms compile
skipped.

